==Czech==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*uxo}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|cs}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂ous-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/uxo/|lang=cs}}
* {{audio|Cs-ucho.ogg|audio|lang=cs}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|g=n}}

# [[ear]]
# [[handle]] {{gloss|of a pot}}
# [[eye]] {{gloss|hole at the blunt end of a needle}}

====Declension====
{{cs-decl-noun-dual|ucho|ucha|uchu|ucho|ucho|uchu|uchem|ucha|uch|uchům|ucha|ucha|uchách|uchy|uši|uší|uším|uši|uši|uších|ušima}}

====Usage notes====
The dual form is used when talking about human or animal ears, no matter of their number (e. g. ''čtyři králičí uši'' = four rabbit ears), while the plural is used when referring to various ear-shaped objects (''ucha hrnce'' = handles of a pot).

